### Pareto Front Assessment (with 10% PolarClean bath, current context)

The current bath is 10 wt% PolarClean. Only experiments run with this bath composition are directly comparable. Filtering to `nips_bath_solvent_wt_percent = 10.0`:

| Condition | Modulus (bar) | Pore Fraction | Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 15-0add-9deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s | 124.3 | 0.55 | Good |
| 14.5-0add-10deg-PolarClean-10wt-200s (run1) | 132.7 | 0.62 | Good |
| 14.5-0add-10deg-PolarClean-10wt-200s (run2) | 105.5 | 0.66 | Good |
| 15.5-0add-9deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s (run2) | 110.7 | 0.59 | Good |
| 15.5-0add-9deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s (run3) | 215.0 | 0.57 | Good |
| 15.5-0add-6deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s (run1) | 159.0 | 0.61 | Minor crease |
| 15.5-0add-6deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s (run2) | 162.8 | 0.73 | Good ✓ |
| 15.5-0add-6deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s (run3) | 215.0 | 0.57 | Good ✓ |
| 15.5-0add-6deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s (run4) | 151.1 | 0.82 | Good ✓ |
| 15.5-0add-5deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s (run1) | 191.5 | 0.62 | Good ✓ |
| 15.5-0add-8deg-PolarClean-10wt-350s | 135.6 | 0.57 | Good ✓ |
| 15-0add-8deg-PolarClean-10wt-200s | 129.3 | 0.49 | Wrinkle |
| 15-0add-8deg-PolarClean-10wt-300s | 147.1 | 0.58 | Top gap |

**Key observations for 10% PolarClean bath:**
- The **15.5 wt% polymer, bath_temp=6°C, 250s wait** condition (runs 2–4) shows the most promising combination: run2 gave modulus=163, PF=0.73; run4 gave modulus=151, PF=0.82. These are among the highest pore fractions seen in this bath.
- Run3 of the same condition gave modulus=215, PF=0.57 — higher modulus but lower pore fraction.
- The **15.5 wt%, bath=5°C, 250s** run1 gave modulus=192, PF=0.62 — good but not as high PF as bath=6°C.
- The **14.5 wt%, bath=10°C, 200s** runs gave high PF (0.62–0.66) but lower modulus (~105–133).

**Pareto-front candidates in 10% PolarClean bath:**
- High PF frontier: 15.5/6°C/250s (PF~0.73–0.82, modulus~151–163)
- High modulus frontier: 15.5/9°C/250s run3 (modulus=215, PF=0.57)

The 15.5/6°C/250s condition has been run 4 times with variable results (PF: 0.57–0.82, modulus: 151–215). This variability is high and the condition has not been confirmed as reproducibly achieving both high modulus AND high pore fraction simultaneously. Run2 (163 bar, 0.73 PF) and run4 (151 bar, 0.82 PF) are the most attractive, but run3 (215 bar, 0.57 PF) and run1 (159 bar, 0.61 PF) show different behavior. The high CV across runs suggests process variability.

### Validation vs. Exploration Decision

The 15.5/6°C/250s condition has 4 runs but shows high inter-run variability in both objectives. This is not yet a confirmed Pareto-front candidate — the variability is too large to treat it as reproducible. However, 4 runs is already substantial; further repeats of the same condition have diminishing returns without understanding the source of variability.

**Better strategy:** Explore a nearby condition that could clarify the tradeoff and potentially improve both objectives. The data suggests:
- Lower bath temp (5–6°C) with 15–16 wt% polymer and 10% PolarClean bath tends to give higher pore fractions
- Moderate wait times (200–300s) work well
- The 15.5/6°C condition has been explored; trying **polymer_wt=15.5, bath_temp=5°C** (one step colder) with a slightly longer wait (300s) and moderate pullcast speed in the 10% PolarClean bath is a natural Pareto-improvement candidate — it could push pore fraction higher while maintaining modulus, since colder bath typically accelerates phase separation

The **15.5/5°C/300s** combination has not been tried in the 10% PolarClean bath (only 15.5/5°C/250s run1 exists). This is a modest, targeted exploration step.

Additionally, I note that mixing_temp=40°C has been used consistently for 15.5 wt% polymer. This is appropriate (not at max polymer_wt=17, so mixing is needed).

**Expected benefit:** Slightly longer wait time (300s vs 250s) at bath_temp=5°C may allow more solvent evaporation/skin formation before NIPS, potentially increasing pore fraction while the cold bath maintains rapid phase separation for structural integrity. This explores a modestly under-sampled region (300s wait at 5°C bath for 15.5 wt% in 10% PolarClean bath) and could yield a Pareto improvement over the 15.5/5°C/250s run1 result (191 bar, 0.62 PF).

