### Current Bath Context
The next experiment uses **PolarClean 10 wt% NIPS bath** — a partially miscible bath that slows phase separation relative to pure water, generally yielding lower modulus but potentially higher pore fraction compared to pure-water baths at similar polymer concentrations.

### Pareto Front Assessment (both objectives measured, good quality)

Reviewing all experiments with valid measurements for both Elastic Modulus and Pore Fraction under the **current bath (PolarClean 10 wt%)**:

| Condition | Modulus (bar) | Pore Fraction | Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 15-0add-9deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s-N2-1600s (run1) | 246.6 (SD=146!) | 0.77 | CV=0.05, clean |
| 15p5-0add-6deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s-N2-1600s (run2) | 162.8 | 0.73 | CV=0.07, clean |
| 15p5-0add-6deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s-N2-1600s (run4) | 151.1 | 0.82 | CV=0.06, clean |
| 14p8-0add-17deg-bathSolv-none-530s-N2-1425s (run2) | 217.0 | 0.82 | wrinkles |
| 14p5-0add-10deg-PolarClean-10wt-200s-N2-1500s | 132.7 | 0.62 | clean |
| 15p5-0add-8deg-PolarClean-10wt-350s-N2-1600s | 135.6 | 0.57 | clean |

The **15p5-0add-6deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s-N2-1600s** condition (runs 1–4) is the most promising Pareto candidate in the current bath: run2 gave modulus=162.8, PF=0.73; run4 gave modulus=151.1, PF=0.82. Run3 gave modulus=215.0, PF=0.57. These three runs show high variability in both objectives across syntheses — the pore fraction ranges from 0.57 to 0.82 and modulus from 151 to 215. This is not yet reproducibly confirmed as a Pareto-front point.

The **15-0add-9deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s-N2-1600s** run1 showed PF=0.77 with modulus=246.6 but had SD=146 on modulus (extremely high CV), making it unreliable. Only one synthesis exists.

### Validation Policy Check

The **15p5-0add-6deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s-N2-1600s** condition has 4 runs but shows high run-to-run variability (PF: 0.57–0.82, modulus: 151–215 bar). This is a strong Pareto-front candidate in the current bath but not yet confirmed as reproducible. However, 4 runs have already been done — the variability itself is informative and suggests the process is noisy at these conditions.

The **15-0add-9deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s-N2-1600s** condition has only 1 valid run with very high modulus SD. This is a high-priority validation target: it showed the best combined performance (modulus ~247, PF=0.77) but with unreliable fit (SD=146 bar on modulus). A repeat would clarify whether this is a genuine high-performing point or a measurement artifact.

**Recommendation: Validate 15-0add-9deg-PolarClean-10wt-250s-N2-1600s** — this is the single-run candidate with the best apparent two-objective performance in the current bath, but the modulus SD of 146 bar (CV ~59%) makes it untrustworthy. A repeat will either confirm a genuinely excellent Pareto point or reveal it was a fluke.

### Expected Benefit
- If confirmed: modulus ~247 bar + PF ~0.77 would be the best simultaneously high-modulus, high-pore-fraction result in the 10 wt% PolarClean bath
- If not confirmed: narrows the true performance range and informs whether to continue exploring this region
